{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"ERP analysis report (customise title to fit your topic)\"\n",
        "author: \"Your name\"\n",
        "date: today\n",
        "format: \n",
        "    html:\n",
        "        embed-resources: true\n",
        "        toc: true\n",
        "        toc-depth: 3\n",
        "        code-fold: true\n",
        "        theme: flatly # adapt this to a theme of your choice if you'd like\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "    warning: false\n",
        "    message: false\n",
        "bibliography: \"erp_report.bib\"\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Setup"
      ],
      "id": "caa0b0d5"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Specify the required imports for your analysis\n",
        "from pathlib import Path\n",
        "\n",
        "from mini_mne import SimpleRaw, SimpleEpoch, grand_average, plot_evokeds\n",
        "\n",
        "# Note how we can import a custom preprocessing function from a local script\n",
        "from scripts.preproc import preprocess"
      ],
      "id": "8d150b31",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Specify the required paths for your analysis\n",
        "# Note that we now include a folder for saving preprocessed data\n",
        "RAW_PATH = Path(\"data/raw\")\n",
        "PROCESSED_PATH = Path(\"data/processed\")"
      ],
      "id": "e31f15d9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Introduction\n",
        "\n",
        "Provide an introduction to the ERP component of your choice here. This should include a brief literature review -- see report instructions for details.\n",
        "Use appropriate subheadings as required: adapt the ones below, create new ones or delete as needed.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Intro subheading 1\n",
        "\n",
        "### Intro subheading 2\n",
        "\n",
        "## Methods\n",
        "\n",
        "Complete the following subsections using the information from @kappenman2021. Don't forget to mention that the data are from the ERP CORE resource under a Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0). \n",
        "\n",
        "### Participants\n",
        "\n",
        "Provide information on the number of participants and their demographics (sex, age, handedness) as well as the inclusion criteria for the study.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Procedure\n",
        "\n",
        "Describe the task that participants completed. This should be tailored to the task / component that you chose to analyse.\n",
        "\n",
        "### EEG recording\n",
        "\n",
        "Describe the EEG recording parameters: amplifier and type of cap used, electrode positions, CMS / DRL electrode positions, EOG electrode positions, and filter parameters.\n",
        "\n",
        "### Analysis parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "Choose these parameters appropriate for the component that you are analysing. Use those recommended by @kappenman2021; see their Table 1. This holds for all parameters except for the filter parameters; for these, you can stick to the example parameters provided below.\n",
        "Describe the parameters in this section and also modify the code accordingly\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Preprocessing parameters"
      ],
      "id": "8efb5b99"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "FILTER_SETTINGS = {\n",
        "    \"low_cutoff\": 0.1,\n",
        "    \"high_cutoff\": 30.0\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "# This setting re-references to averaged mastoids (P9/P10 as proxy) \n",
        "# To use an average reference, replace [\"P9\", \"P10\"] with None \n",
        "REFERENCE = [\"P9\",\"P10\"]"
      ],
      "id": "c26b94e1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#### Epoching parameters"
      ],
      "id": "c56cc326"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "TMIN = -0.2 # epoch start relative to critical event\n",
        "TMAX = 1.0  # epoch end relative to critical event\n",
        "\n",
        "BASELINE = (-0.2,0) # baseline interval\n",
        "\n",
        "# critical conditions for averaging and epoching\n",
        "CONDITIONS = [\"stimulus/compatible\", \"stimulus/incompatible\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "REJECT = {\n",
        "    \"eeg\": 150e-6,\n",
        "    \"eog\": 250e-6\n",
        "}"
      ],
      "id": "d18679df",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Data analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "### Preprocessing"
      ],
      "id": "b291d912"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| eval: true # set this to false if you don't want preprocessing to recompute\n",
        "#| output: false # this suppresses any output\n",
        "\n",
        "for raw_file in RAW_PATH.glob(\"*_raw.fif.gz\"):\n",
        "\n",
        "    # extract subject number\n",
        "    subj_ID = raw_file.stem.split(\"_\")[0]\n",
        "\n",
        "    # read in raw file \n",
        "    raw = SimpleRaw(raw_file)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # preprocess raw file\n",
        "    # note how we draw on a custom preprocessing function here\n",
        "    processed = preprocess(raw, \n",
        "                            reref_params = REFERENCE, \n",
        "                            filter_low_cutoff = FILTER_SETTINGS[\"low_cutoff\"], \n",
        "                            filter_high_cutoff = FILTER_SETTINGS[\"high_cutoff\"])\n",
        "    \n",
        "    processed.save(PROCESSED_PATH / f\"{subj_ID}_raw.fif.gz\", overwrite = True)\n"
      ],
      "id": "1f1436a2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Epoching and averaging"
      ],
      "id": "4a2d5e5a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| output: false\n",
        "\n",
        "# initialise empty dictionary to hold single-subject averages\n",
        "ss_avs = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for cond in CONDITIONS:\n",
        "    ss_avs[cond] = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for processed_file in PROCESSED_PATH.glob(\"*_raw.fif.gz\"):\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # read in preprocessed file\n",
        "    processed = SimpleRaw(processed_file)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # extract events\n",
        "    events, event_id = processed.get_events()\n",
        "\n",
        "    # epoch data\n",
        "    epochs = SimpleEpoch(processed, events, event_id, tmin = TMIN, tmax = TMAX, baseline = BASELINE, reject = REJECT)\n",
        "\n",
        "    # subset epochs and average by condition \n",
        "    for cond in CONDITIONS:\n",
        "        av = epochs[cond].average()\n",
        "        ss_avs[cond].append(av)"
      ],
      "id": "5e0c6d59",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Grand average"
      ],
      "id": "9096e91d"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "#| output: false\n",
        "\n",
        "# create an empty dict to hold our grand averages\n",
        "grand_avs = {}\n",
        "\n",
        "for cond in CONDITIONS:\n",
        "    grand = grand_average(ss_avs[cond])\n",
        "    grand_avs[cond] = grand"
      ],
      "id": "3b354e5a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Results\n",
        "\n",
        "### Grand average: expected effect\n",
        "\n",
        "Plot the electrode deemed most representative for the effect by @kappenman2021.\n",
        "Set the parameters for the specified analysis window, which will include dotted vertical lines marking the analysis window on the plot.\n",
        "Note: for some components, @kappenman2021 refer to two electrode sites. If this is the case for your chosen component, the analysis requires a consideration of lateralisation; please make an appointment to discuss the required analysis tweaks with Ina."
      ],
      "id": "9c62234c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "selected_electrode = \"FCz\"\n",
        "plot_title = \"Grand average for N2: Incompatible versus compatible Flanker stimuli\"\n",
        "analysis_window_start = 0.2\n",
        "analysis_window_end = 0.4\n",
        "\n",
        "plot_evokeds(grand_avs, picks = selected_electrode, invert_y = True, title = plot_title, vlines = [analysis_window_start, analysis_window_end])\n"
      ],
      "id": "8703fc87",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Discussion and reflection\n",
        "\n",
        "Provide a brief discussion of the effect that you observed. Were you able to replicate the ERP component as observed by @kappenman2021? If not, what was different in your grand average ERP? \n",
        "\n",
        "What did you learn by applying the analysis process to a new dataset?\n",
        "\n",
        "## References\n",
        "\n",
        "*Note: this document is set up to automatically generate a reference list via a bib file. We will look at how to do this in the week 9 workshop.*\n"
      ],
      "id": "b6861da1"
    }
  ],
